Comic Relief lettering for the camera's icon font (/usr/share/app/Sony_DI_Icons.ttf)

The icons draw their lettering (AWB, MF, ISO, PP1 ...) as plain outline contours. These scripts find
those letters and swap them for Comic Relief Bold ones, each icon staying inside its own bytes:

  export ICONS=Sony_DI_Icons.ttf  LTT=UniversOTS-SJ_wIcon.ltt   # the camera's own files (not included)
  export COMIC=ComicRelief-Bold.ttf                               # SIL Open Font License 1.1
  python3 shapes.py     # every icon split into shapes (a contour and the contours right inside it)
  python3 classify.py   # each shape compared with letters of a few reference fonts (Univers from LTT, plus
                        # DejaVu Sans Condensed Bold, Liberation Sans Narrow Bold, Carlito Bold if installed)
  python3 runs.py       # only shapes standing in a line of text count as letters
  python3 icons.py      # icons.ttf (to look at), icons.patch.json (for ../mkheader.py)
  python3 pages.py      # optional: page*.png, before/after sheets of every changed icon

fixshapes.json holds corrections made by eye ("glyph:contour": letter, or null for "not a letter").
Icons whose letters are very narrow (video formats like 1080/60p) or whose Comic version doesn't fit
in the icon's bytes keep their own lettering, as do plain bars (I, 1, the stem of an i).

